Package: scagg
Type: Package
Title: Pseudobulk and Metacell Aggregation for Single-Cell RNA-seq
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2026-10-15
Authors@R: person("Ethan", "Fenton",
                  email = "ethanfenton27@gmail.com",
                  role  = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides three aggregation strategies for single-cell RNA-seq
    Seurat objects: (1) true pseudobulk aggregation (one sample per unique
    group combination), (2) metacell creation by target cell size, and (3)
    metacell creation by target metacell count per group. Metacells can be
    formed randomly or from transcriptionally similar cells via balanced
    recursive bisection of an embedding, keeping metacell sizes balanced.
    All functions accept user-specified grouping and metadata variables and
    produce a full cell-to-metacell traceability table.
